From 508d66375c2ab03f279c4cb6893ad9762780b1c0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "Michael C. Ferguson" <michael.christopher.ferguson@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 25 Sep 2026 15:05:28 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 2/6] usb: dwc2: hcd_ddma: unmap the frame list with the
 direction it was mapped

The descriptor DMA frame list is only written by the CPU and read by
the controller, and dwc2_frame_list_alloc() maps it DMA_TO_DEVICE, as
do the dma_sync_single_for_device() calls in dwc2_update_frame_list().
dwc2_frame_list_free() however unmaps it DMA_FROM_DEVICE.

The DMA API requires the unmap direction to match the mapping, and
CONFIG_DMA_API_DEBUG reports the mismatch. On non-coherent systems an
unmap for DMA_FROM_DEVICE also invalidates the CPU cache over the
buffer, which is pointless for memory the device never writes.

Use DMA_TO_DEVICE for the unmap as well.

Fixes: 95105a998dff ("usb: dwc2: host: avoid usage of dma_alloc_coherent with irqs disabled")
Signed-off-by: Michael C. Ferguson <michael.christopher.ferguson@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/usb/dwc2/hcd_ddma.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/usb/dwc2/hcd_ddma.c b/drivers/usb/dwc2/hcd_ddma.c
index ce40a4f..5ec6e79 100644
--- a/drivers/usb/dwc2/hcd_ddma.c
+++ b/drivers/usb/dwc2/hcd_ddma.c
@@ -140,7 +140,7 @@ static void dwc2_frame_list_free(struct dwc2_hsotg *hsotg)
 	}
 
 	dma_unmap_single(hsotg->dev, hsotg->frame_list_dma,
-			 hsotg->frame_list_sz, DMA_FROM_DEVICE);
+			 hsotg->frame_list_sz, DMA_TO_DEVICE);
 
 	kfree(hsotg->frame_list);
 	hsotg->frame_list = NULL;
